{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KbzYCmGgySXfbFeuhVtHsC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven pipeline that generates Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils from formal PRDs, then verifies them via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Human writes PRDs and use cases → mage-claude-orchestrator generates Go code in cmd/ and pkg/ → differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) verifies output parity against GNU reference binaries. Shared packages: pkg/sys (syscalls), pkg/format (formatting), pkg/testutils (test harness).\n\n**Implementation status:** Releases 00.0 through 05.1 are spec_complete or implemented (code at generation tags). Release 05.2 (cut, paste) has spec_complete status with no code yet.\n\n**Current release:** rel05.2 — columnar operations pair (cut, paste). Both use cases are spec_complete, code not started.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 05.2 is the earliest incomplete release. Cut comes before paste alphabetically. Per P2, implementation and tests are separate tasks. With a 1-task limit, I propose cmd/cut implementation first — paste can follow in the next batch.\n\nCut is a standalone utility with no pkg/ dependencies beyond sys (SIGPIPE) and testutils (tests, deferred to separate task). It follows the same cmd/ pattern as basename, dirname, and other simple utilities already generated.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/cut -- prd-cut R1-R4: selection modes, delimiters, file handling, exit codes\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find and read the PRD for cut, named prd*-cut.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.2-uc001-cut.yaml\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.2.yaml (cut test cases for behavioral reference)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section -- differential testing pattern and SIGPIPE handling)\n      - cmd/head/main.go (reference for a simple stream-processing utility -- match code style and structure)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cut/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"cut utility implementation: flag parsing, range parsing, field/byte/character selection, multi-file processing\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement the three selection modes from the cut PRD: byte selection (-b),\n          character selection (-c), and field selection (-f). Parse range specifications\n          (N, N-M, N-, -M) and comma-separated lists. Exactly one of -b, -c, -f is\n          required; error if none or more than one is given.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement delimiter and output control from the cut PRD: input delimiter (-d,\n          default TAB for -f mode), suppress lines without delimiters (-s, only with -f),\n          and output delimiter (--output-delimiter, defaults to input delimiter). For -b\n          and -c modes, -d and -s are errors.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement file handling: read from files listed on the command line, or stdin\n          if no files given or file is \"-\". Concatenate output across files in order.\n          Support \"--\" to end option parsing.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement exit codes, --version, --help, SIGPIPE handling, and error reporting.\n          Exit 0 on success, 1 on error. Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the\n          start of main(). Write errors to stderr with \"cut: \" prefix. Support\n          --complement flag to invert the selected range.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Follow the shared_protocols SIGPIPE pattern from ARCHITECTURE.yaml:\n          call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main().\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Match the code style and structure of cmd/head/main.go or another existing\n          simple stream utility. Use flag or pflag consistent with existing cmd/ packages.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Range parsing produces a sorted, merged list of 1-based column/byte/field\n          indices. Process each input line by selecting the specified positions and\n          joining with the output delimiter.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Do NOT create tests in this task. Tests will be a separate task. Do NOT\n          install any packages -- use only the Go standard library plus pkg/sys.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/cut/main.go exists and compiles: `go build ./cmd/cut/` succeeds with no errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"All three selection modes work: `echo 'a:b:c' | go run ./cmd/cut/ -d: -f2` prints 'b'.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Range parsing handles N, N-M, N-, -M, and comma-separated lists correctly.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"--complement inverts the selection. -s suppresses lines without delimiter in -f mode.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Multiple files are processed in order; stdin is used when no files are given.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Exit code is 0 on success, 1 on errors. Errors are written to stderr with 'cut: ' prefix.\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() is called at the start of main().\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27528,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27528},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"533457c1-4212-47b0-a05d-c97d35754711","uuid":"96f13e30-13c6-4559-b851-80bb60ae8fbc"}
